# T4. The arm isn't where the skill starts (it is at its power-on angles; the sample starts at the `ready` pose, 30°
# away at the elbow): refused not_at_start at once, before anyone is asked to press Confirm, and an offer of it is
# dropped. The terminal's reason names the pose to go to first (test/motion.test.ts checks the words). Once the
# arm is at `ready`, the same skill is asked about.
expect motion mode ready
key torque-on-left
wait 2100
key c
expect motion torque left on
key skill-run-sample
expect motion command skill.run refused:not_at_start operator_cli
absent 2500 motion target skill.run
key offer-skill-sample
expect sim offer dropped
key pose-ready-left
wait 2100
key c
expect 5000 motion command arm.go_to_pose completed operator_cli
key skill-run-sample
expect motion target skill.run operator_cli: SIMULATED sample: hold it out
key q
